For any $n \in \{1,\ldots,49\}$, a \emph{middle vertex} of 
$L_n$ is a vertex that is $n+1$ edges away from two corners of $L_n$, 
which are end vertices of some side path of $L_n$. 
%both of the 
%end vertices of some side path of $L_n$.  
\emph{The} middle vertex of a side path $B$ of $L_n$ is the vertex of $L_n$
that lies at the midpoint of $B$.  Given any pentagonal face
$U$, a \emph{spoke} of $U$ is a path of length $98$ connecting
a vertex on $L_{U,49}$ and the centre of $U$. % We write
%$v_1 \xrightarrow{F_1} v_2 \xrightarrow{F_2} v_3 \xrightarrow{F_3} \ldots
%v_n \xrightarrow{F_n} v_{n+1}$ to denote a transition
